  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting all incidents within 24 hours and customer notice within 72 hours, with no delay for root cause. S2 sets a 55 °C test and a 5% action threshold, but sales restrictions only after remediation and a regulator finding; per-model results go to customers and regulators but not the public. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 36 months and retrofit to 6 years, S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months, and S5 uses an 8/100k review trigger while leaving recall to regulator discretion."
